From: Wasmer Engineering <engineering@wasmer.io>
Subject: [PATCH] Only hide Apple new/delete symbols with bundled libc++

Apple's system libc++ declares operator new/delete with default visibility.
Forcing hidden visibility in the allocator shim conflicts with those
declarations in the macOS 26 SDK. Only force hidden visibility when using
bundled libc++, which is built with the matching visibility setting.

diff --git a/third_party/partition_alloc/src/partition_alloc/BUILD.gn b/third_party/partition_alloc/src/partition_alloc/BUILD.gn
--- a/third_party/partition_alloc/src/partition_alloc/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/partition_alloc/src/partition_alloc/BUILD.gn
@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@
 # Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
 # found in the LICENSE file.
 
+import("//build/config/c++/c++.gni")
+
 import("../../partition_alloc.gni")
 import("buildflag_header.gni")
 
@@ -367,7 +369,9 @@
   }
 
   config("mac_no_default_new_delete_symbols") {
-    if (!is_component_build) {
+    if (!is_component_build && use_custom_libcxx) {
+      # System libc++ declares these symbols with default visibility, which
+      # conflicts with force-hidden. Only hide them with bundled libc++.
       # This is already set when we compile libc++, see
       # buildtools/third_party/libc++/BUILD.gn. But it needs to be set here as
       # well, since the shim defines the symbols, to prevent them being
